# Worker, not keys — LOCKED

Do not give ChatGPT, Grok, or any third-party chat R2 admin keys, Cloudflare
account credentials, or `~/.config/r2/env`. Point them at the Worker:

`https://litigation-doc-api.ss8sxswwkt.workers.dev`

Read routes stay open without credentials (`/health`, `/matters`,
`/fuse`, `/upcoming`, `/doc/<sha256>`, `/documents/<path>`, `/mcp`) except
the 14-path private denylist in
`internal/src/data/documents/private-documents.json`. Do not add a blanket
auth gate on `/doc`.

The Worker is the API in front of R2. Keys stay server-side in the `DOCS`
binding. Pasting admin keys into a chatbot sends them to someone else's
servers, into logs, possibly into training data. There is no unsee.

- **Cursor on the laptop:** source `~/.config/r2/env` for writes
  (`documents:push`), or call the Worker like everyone else for reads.
  No keys in chat, no git, no Actions.
- **If a chat needs a secret at all:** one rotatable Worker bearer on the
  read routes — not the Cloudflare keys. If something truly needs direct
  R2, mint a **read-only** token scoped to `litigation-documents` and
  revoke it if it leaks. Never share the admin pair.
- Admin keys live in exactly two places: the laptop `~/.config/r2/env`
  (mode 600) and the Worker's bindings.

Portfolio-wide. Cursor, Claude Code, Copilot, and any other agent reading
this repo.
